            <ArticleTitle>[Pharmacodynamics of allapinine during long-term infusion in patients with chronic ischemic heart disease and frequent ventricular extrasystole].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>58-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During a prolonged (24-hour) intravenous administration in a dose of 126 mg, allapinine produced a stable pronounced antiarrhythmic effect in 90% of the patients with frequent premature ventricular contraction and adverse reactions in the central nervous system in 65% of the cases. However, the latter effect of allapinine is short-term and ceased independently without altering the infusion rate. More serious adverse effects (hypotensive reactions, proarhythmic effects) occurred in 4% of the cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
